  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The RMT union initiated a 24-hour strike across the London Underground network today, following unsuccessful negotiations regarding pay and working conditions. Commuters across the capital face potential travel disruptions as the walkout affects various service lines. RMT official Eddie Dempsey has publicly called on the Mayor of London, Sadiq Khan, to intervene in the ongoing dispute. Despite the strike action, Transport for London confirmed that some service continues to operate, noting that the Piccadilly line has seen drivers reporting for duty, with plans for that specific line to remain functional until 9pm. Passengers are being advised by transport officials to check for real-time updates and plan their travel arrangements carefully while the industrial action remains in effect. The current situation follows a period of failed talks that preceded the start of this planned 24-hour industrial stoppage.",
